<title>USA: IBM expected to issue $1.0 bln debt.</title>
<headline>IBM expected to issue $1.0 bln debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Business Machines Corp is expected to tap the corporate bond primary market with a $1.0 billion two-part debt offering, dealers said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The first tranche is expected to include $500 million of a 10-year bullet issue. Price talk is seen in the low 40 basis points area, dealers said.</p>
<p>The second tranche is expected to include $500 million in 30-year debt, putable in seven years, with price talk seen 18-20 basis points over Treasuries.</p>
<p>Morgan Stanley Dean Witter is expected to underwrite the debt offering, the fealers said.</p>
<p>((--Nancy Leinfuss, U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1675))</p>
